<title>GERMANY: Krones ups profits, sales in 1996.</title>
<headline>Krones ups profits, sales in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			  27	 vs 13</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities   58	 vs 36</p>
<p>    Group DVFA earnings per share    21.07	 vs 3.79 marks</p>
<p>    Group sales			    1,631	 vs 1,579</p>
<p>    Group orders			   1,236	 vs 1,349</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			  105	 vs 81</p>
<p>    Dividend (ordinaries)		 5.50	 vs 5.50 marks</p>
<p>    Dividend (preferreds)		 7.50	 vs 7.50 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German packaging machinery group is Krones AG Hermann Kronseder Maschinenfabrik, Neutraubling.</p>
<p>The company said that sales and earnings were in line with targets during the first five months of this year, but orders had fallen significantly.</p>
<p>Krones also expects to achieve sales and earnings this year in line with 1996, and plans to double its return on capital by the year 2000.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
